```json
{
  "schemaVersion": "0.3.0-alpha",
  "programId": "hek293-passaging-two-flasks",
  "name": "Passaging two T75 flasks of adherent HEK293 (1:6 into four)",
  "description": "Two T75 flasks at ~90% confluence, split 1:6 into four new flasks. The per-flask chain (rinse, trypsinise, neutralise, spin, resuspend, count, seed) is ONE replicated step chain: count 2, so flask B releases the moment flask A leaves the cabinet. The cabinet, centrifuge and microscope are single-occupancy (maxConcurrent 1) and do the queueing; the CO2 incubator holds both flasks at once (maxConcurrent 2). One operator. Target: both pairs seeded within ~1 h, then >=16 h settling, then cleanup and log.",
  "environmentType": "laboratory",
  "actors": 1,
  "tracks": [
    {
      "trackId": "culture",
      "name": "Culture work — cabinet, incubator, centrifuge, microscope",
      "steps": [
        {
          "stepId": "prep-cabinet",
          "name": "Wipe cabinet, lay out pipettes and tubes, run blower",
          "task": "cabinet",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 600 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "programStart" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "check-confluence",
          "name": "Check both flasks for confluence and contamination",
          "task": "microscope",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 600 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "prep-cabinet" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "rinse-pbs",
          "name": "Aspirate spent medium, rinse monolayer with 5 mL PBS",
          "task": "cabinet",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 240 },
          "replicates": { "count": 2, "mode": "parallel" },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "check-confluence" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "trypsinise",
          "name": "Add 2 mL trypsin-EDTA, rock flask, incubate 5 min",
          "task": "incubator",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 300 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "rinse-pbs", "instances": "each" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "neutralise",
          "name": "Knock flask, check detachment, neutralise with 8 mL medium",
          "task": "cabinet",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 300 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "trypsinise", "instances": "each" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "spin",
          "name": "Transfer to 15 mL tube, spin 300 x g for 5 min",
          "task": "centrifuge",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 300 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "neutralise", "instances": "each" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "resuspend",
          "name": "Aspirate supernatant, resuspend pellet in 10 mL fresh medium",
          "task": "cabinet",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 240 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "spin", "instances": "each" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "count-cells",
          "name": "Count cells on haemocytometer",
          "task": "microscope",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 360 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "resuspend", "instances": "each" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "seed-flasks",
          "name": "Seed two new T75 flasks at 1:6 and label them",
          "task": "cabinet",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 360 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "count-cells", "instances": "each" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "settle-overnight",
          "name": "Return all four new flasks to the incubator to settle (>=16 h)",
          "task": "incubator",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 57600 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "seed-flasks", "instances": "all" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "wipe-down",
          "name": "Wipe cabinet down, discard waste, blower to standby",
          "task": "cabinet",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 600 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "settle-overnight" }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "culture-log",
          "name": "Log passage number, split ratio and counts",
          "task": "bench",
          "duration": { "type": "fixed", "seconds": 300 },
          "startTrigger": { "type": "afterStep", "stepId": "wipe-down" }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "resourceConstraints": [
    { "task": "cabinet", "maxConcurrent": 1 },
    { "task": "centrifuge", "maxConcurrent": 1 },
    { "task": "microscope", "maxConcurrent": 1 },
    { "task": "incubator", "maxConcurrent": 2 },
    { "task": "bench", "maxConcurrent": 1 }
  ]
}
```

Design notes (tooling unavailable offline, so no live URL this pass — run this through `validate_program` → `analyze_schedule` → `visualize_schedule` when the Rhylthyme tools are reachable):

- **Repeated work, not copied JSON**: the whole per-flask chain hangs off ONE replicated step (`rinse-pbs`, `replicates: {count: 2, mode: "parallel"}`); `trypsinise → neutralise → spin → resuspend → count-cells → seed-flasks` all use `instances: "each"`, so flask B releases the moment flask A leaves the cabinet. `settle-overnight` is the explicit `"all"` barrier that waits for both seeded pairs.
- **Limits as constraints**: cabinet, centrifuge and haemocytometer/microscope are `maxConcurrent: 1` and do all the queueing (cabinet is expected to be the binding constraint); the CO₂ incubator is `maxConcurrent: 2` because both flasks — and later all four new flasks — sit in it together. One operator is `actors: 1`.
- **No `maxInFlight` needed**: nothing here is a fixed-size holding rack between a step and its barrier (the incubator accepts both flasks), so the in-flight cap would have nothing to hold back.
- **Makespan**: ~61 min of bench work (cabinet-gated) + 16 h settling + 15 min cleanup/log ≈ 16 h 17 m; if you want the four flasks seeded tighter, the cabinet is the only lever, since it is the sole serialising resource.
